{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7D5yExt6w9t9eSi2Su9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\nSubject: What we changed after last summer's hail\n\nHi [First name],\n\nYou didn't renew your share this year, and I think I know why.\n\nOn July 9, a hailstorm destroyed about half our crops. For the next six weeks, your boxes had about half the usual amount. We didn't offer refunds or credit, and I sent only one short email about it. That wasn't good enough. You paid for full boxes, and you deserved a clear explanation and a better response from me.\n\nHere's what we've changed:\n\n- **A second field on higher ground**, so our crops aren't all in one place.\n- **Two hail nets** over our tomatoes and peppers.\n- **Pause credits:** you can now pause up to two weeks and get credit for them.\n\nThe new field and nets cost us $31,000. A full share is still $540, the same as last year, with pickup every Thursday for 22 weeks.\n\nSign-up closes March 15, and 52 shares are left. If you'd like to come back, you can sign up here: [link]\n\nIf you'd rather tell me what would bring you back, just reply to this email.\n\nThank you for the seasons you spent with us.\n\n[Your name]\n[Farm name]\n</final_document>\n\nThe email is about 190 words. It says plainly what went wrong and owns how you handled it. I left it to the facts you gave me. It doesn't promise the nets will stop hail damage, and it doesn't say why the higher field helps. If there's a real reason you can state, like better drainage or a different storm track, adding one line about it would make that point stronger. Before sending, fill in the name merge field, the sign-up link and your signature."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5357,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tok